# What `gcloud run deploy --source server` must not upload.
#
# gcloud looks for this file in the upload root — this folder — and consults
# neither the repository's .gitignore (a level up, outside the root) nor
# .dockerignore (which applies to the build context, after the upload). So
# everything excluded has to be listed here too, not only there.
#
# data/ is the reason this file exists: PGlite writes its local database with
# 1970 timestamps, and a source upload is a ZIP, whose format cannot carry a
# date before 1980. With the folder present the deploy dies on
# "ZIP does not support timestamps before 1980" partway through uploading.
# The deployed server never reads it — it reaches Postgres over DATABASE_URL —
# so it has no business in the image either way.

node_modules/
dist/
data/
.env
.env.*
*.log
